From a908858906cba14784111fe10d33f1e767211948 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 02:01:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dvbridge: the layers of a Dolby Vision video and the RPU of
 its first picture, in the log once a video

Once a video, in kodi.log without debugging, whichever bridge draws it (native output, or Dolby
Vision reconstructed for output as HDR10): of each layer, its size, its layout and bits as decoded,
the size of its textures as the bridge was given them (said when they are not of the picture's
size) and where its chroma sits; how the enhancement layer stands to the base, and what the decoder
made of it (its pool of surfaces, and the dma-buf that the bridge imports: the format of each plane,
the modifier, the pitches, the objects), or why there is none with the picture (not decoded, or set
aside because its RPU carries no residual); and of the RPU of that picture, the profile that its
header is of as FFmpeg reads one (ff_dovi_guess_profile_hevc()), whether its NLQ adds a residual
(FEL) or nothing (MEL, the rule of dvbridge_mel.h), its coefficients, the reshaping of each
component, its mapping and its resampling filters. Bits are said against the RPU only where a layer
holds fewer than the RPU declares.

What the line of the first picture of each native output, the line of the first reconstructed
picture and the decoder's line of the stream already say is not said again. GL texture names are
not logged: they tell nothing past one run.

The idea is CroqueMr's: the first-frame line of his build (R1.0.0-RC1.1-Debug) gives the size of
each layer and of its textures, and where its chroma sits.

A layer that the renderer sets aside (its RPU carries no residual) is now passed to
PrepareHardware(), which sets it aside itself, as the caller did, so that its size can be told;
nothing changes in what is drawn.

The line is made by DVBridgeLayers.h, which decides nothing; a host test runs it (71 checks, also
with ASan and UBSan, and 16 mutations of the header, each of which makes it fail). Keyed on the
same count of videos as the automatic choice of the content mapping v4.0.
